input.new_string:
/* Drop cap on the very first paragraph — the magazine touch.
 *
 * `::first-letter` beats the inline `font-family` / `font-size` that the
 * type controls write onto the surrounding span, so anything hard-coded
 * here is a rule the writer cannot override. Setting a manuscript in
 * Special Elite used to leave its most prominent glyph in Fraunces.
 *
 * `font-family: inherit` puts the letter back under the writer's control.
 * The size stays proportional — a drop cap that ignored the type scale
 * would be worse — but it is bounded: 4.2em of 36pt is ~200px, which
 * overflows the sheet. The cap sits just above 4.2em of the default 18px
 * body, so the house look is unchanged until the writer goes large. */
.twyne-editor .ProseMirror > p:first-of-type::first-letter {
  font-family: inherit;
  font-weight: 700;
  font-size: min(4.2em, 5rem);
  float: left;
  line-height: 0.85;
  margin: 0.08em 0.12em -0.05em 0;
  color: var(--color-vermilion);
}

